{"annotator_prompt": [
  {"kind": "delete", "field": "blue_cube_pos"},
  {"kind": "delete", "field": "green_cube_pos"},
  {"kind": "delete", "field": "red_cube_pos"},
  {"kind": "add", "field": "goal_cube_positions", "description": "Ordered list of the [y, x] positions of the cubes named in the goal instruction, in the order the goal names them, as those cubes were seen at step #1 (t=0) while loose and before any container has come down. One entry per cube the goal names (one entry for a one-container goal, two for a two-container goal); cubes the goal does not name are not recorded. Written at step #1 and held unchanged for the rest of the episode, even after a cube is hidden by a container or briefly re-exposed when a container is lifted. e.g. [[78, 157], [106, 105]] for a goal that names the blue cube then the red cube."}
],
 "policy_prompt_for_memory": [
  {"kind": "delete", "field": "blue_cube_pos"},
  {"kind": "delete", "field": "green_cube_pos"},
  {"kind": "delete", "field": "red_cube_pos"},
  {"kind": "add", "field": "goal_cube_positions", "description": "Ordered list of the [y, x] positions of the cubes the goal instruction names, in the goal's order. If this step shows loose cubes and no containers anywhere (the scene before the button is pressed), read the goal, take each cube it names in order, and write that cube's [y, x] as shown; skip cubes the goal does not name. Otherwise copy the carried-in list unchanged; never overwrite an entry from a cube briefly exposed under a lifted container. e.g. [[78, 157], [106, 105]] when the goal names blue then red."}
],
 "policy_prompt_for_subgoal": [
  {"modify_from": "choose A (press the button); at the same time record each cube's position in the memory fields.", "modify_to": "choose A (press the button); at the same time record goal_cube_positions: the [y, x] of each cube the goal names, in the goal's order."},
  {"modify_from": "The target is the cube named in the goal at position picks_done+1 in the goal's order (first named cube when picks_done is 0, second named cube when picks_done is 1). Look up that cube's recorded position (blue_cube_pos / green_cube_pos / red_cube_pos) and point at the center of the container nearest to that recorded position", "modify_to": "The target position is the entry of goal_cube_positions at index picks_done (first entry when picks_done is 0, second entry when picks_done is 1). Point at the center of the container nearest to that recorded position"},
  {"modify_from": "Ignore containers that cover no recorded cube.", "modify_to": "Ignore containers that cover no recorded position."},
  {"modify_from": "otherwise B at the container nearest the last named cube.", "modify_to": "otherwise B at the container nearest the last entry of goal_cube_positions."},
  {"modify_from": "choose B at the container nearest the recorded position of the next goal cube", "modify_to": "choose B at the container nearest the entry of goal_cube_positions at index picks_done (the last entry if picks_done is beyond the list)"}
],
 "refused": "Nothing in the report is refused. The round scored perfectly, so the field substitution is committed as a necessity cleanup only: the three per-colour fields each go unread whenever their colour is absent from the goal, and the goal is repeated at every step, so a goal-ordered list indexed by picks_done carries exactly what Rule 2 reads. The picks_done wording from round 1 is untouched, and the subgoal rules keep the same transitions with only the lookup replaced, so no earlier edit is undone."}
